## 5. FRONTEND ARCHITECTURE & COMPONENT BREAKDOWN

### 5.1 Routing (React Router v6 in `App.js`) [INFERRED]
Wrap the app in `<BrowserRouter><AuthProvider>`. Layout: `<Navbar/>` on top, `<main className="min-h-screen">` with `<Routes>`, a simple footer (`© StudyGlobe`).

| Path | Page | Access |
|---|---|---|
| `/` | Home | public |
| `/login` | Login | public (redirect to `/` if already logged in) |
| `/register` | Register | public (same redirect) |
| `/profile` | Profile | `<ProtectedRoute>` |
| `/countries` | Countries | public |
| `/universities` | Universities (supports `?country_id=`, `?search=` and all filters in query string) | public |
| `/universities/:id` | UniversityDetails | public |
| `/programs` | Programs | public |
| `/admin` | Admin | `<ProtectedRoute adminOnly>` |
| `*` | NotFound (inline simple component in App.js: "Page not found" + link home) | public |

### 5.2 API client (`services/api.js`) [SOURCE: "Axios instance + token interceptors"]
- `const api = axios.create({ baseURL: process.env.REACT_APP_API_URL || '/api', timeout: 20000 })`.
- **Storage keys** (localStorage) [DECIDED]: `sg_access_token`, `sg_refresh_token`, `sg_user`.
- **Request interceptor:** if an access token exists, set `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
- **Response interceptor:** on `401` for a request that is not `/auth/login`, `/auth/register` or `/auth/refresh` and has not been retried: call `POST /auth/refresh` once (single in-flight promise shared by concurrent requests), store new tokens, retry the original request. If refresh fails → clear storage and `window.location.assign('/login')`.
- **Network failure** (`!error.response`): reject with `Error("Cannot reach the server. Is the backend running?")` [SOURCE troubleshooting text: "Cannot reach the server"].
- Normalise other errors to `Error(error.response.data.error || 'Something went wrong')`.
- Export small helpers, one per endpoint, returning `response.data`: `authApi.{register,login,me}`, `profileApi.{get,update}`, `countriesApi.{list,get}`, `universitiesApi.{list,get,byCountry}`, `programsApi.{list,get,fields,byUniversity}`, `intakesApi.byUniversity`, `languageApi.byUniversity`, `scholarshipsApi.{list,byUniversity,assess}`, `adminApi.{list,create,update,remove}`.

### 5.3 State management (`context/AuthContext.js`) [SOURCE: AuthContext]
React Context only. Provides `{ user, profile, isAuthenticated, isAdmin, loading, login(email,pw), register(email,pw,fullName), logout(), updateProfile(fields), refreshProfile() }`.
- On mount: if an access token exists, call `GET /auth/me`; success → set user/profile; failure → clear. `loading` is `true` until this completes (ProtectedRoute shows a spinner meanwhile).
- `login`/`register` store `access_token`, `refresh_token`, user; set profile from the response.
- `isAdmin = Boolean(profile?.is_admin)`.
- `logout` clears storage and state and navigates to `/`.

